  "objective_summary": "Landed ParallelFrontier@1 as a pure planning leaf that enforces every readiness condition fail-closed (active plan, legal lifecycle, predecessors, semantic binding, capsule/source fallback, contracts/obligations, scope, conflicts, resources, provider capacity, completion policy, quarantine, supersession, block, review, and model authority), computes the ready set, projects the dedicated conflict graph, and selects a resource-feasible conflict-free antichain with deterministic bounded integer scoring. Small frontiers use exact search; larger frontiers use greedy-plus-local-improvement. Antichain rank is width, then integer score, then stable task identity, so a single high-score conflicting task cannot shrink a wider feasible wave and negative resource costs cannot prefer the empty set. Explicit zero age/retry/provider-pressure arguments are distinct from omitted values that fall back to task payload fields. Model proposals remain non-authoritative and never admit work. Binary floats are excluded from content-addressed selection identities. Worker completion or task status alone never authorizes acceptance.",
